+/*
+ * Adreno 630 (A630, SDM845, OnePlus 6T "fajita") power-up and kernel client.
+ *
+ * The A530 driver for the Pixel (joranv1/ios-sailfish, bsd/dev/sweet_gpu_a530.c)
+ * is the model for this file: same boot-arg, same SweetGPU client, same
+ * service thread shape.  The register programming is A6xx and follows
+ * mainline Linux (drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gpu.c, a6xx_gmu.c,
+ * a6xx_hfi.c, a6xx_catalog.c), gpucc-sdm845.c, gcc-sdm845.c, the Adreno
+ * SMMU driver, qcom_scm/qcom_mdt_loader and the sdm845.dtsi description.
+ * Thanks to joranv1/ios-sailfish for the A530 driver this is built on.
+ *
+ * sweetgpu=0 (default) does nothing.  Levels (see FAJITA.md):
+ *   1  GCC/GPUCC clocks, CX GDSC, GPU id from the catalog; no GPU register
+ *      access (the GX domain is still off).
+ *   2  adds SMMU, GMU boot (firmware, RPMh votes, HFI) and GPU register
+ *      readbacks (VBIF_VERSION, RBBM_STATUS, ...).
+ *   3  adds the command processor, zap shader, compute self-test.
+ *   8  service mode: no boot pauses, full API self-test, GPU on for userland.
+ *
+ * Firmware is extracted from the phone (tools/fajita-gpu-fw.py) and handed
+ * over in the payload as GPU-SQE, GPU-GMU and GPU-ZAP; nothing is embedded
+ * here.  The only embedded program is the Mesa ir3 sample4 compute shader
+ * used by sweet_gpu_quad and by the level-3 self-test.
+ *
+ * Deliberate omissions (all would need IRQs, runtime PM or firmware data
+ * that this port does not use yet; polling replaces them):
+ *   - no interrupts: RBBM/GMU interrupt masks are set to a quiet state and
+ *     fences are polled from kernel memory;
+ *   - no runtime PM/slumber: the GPU stays on after bring-up;
+ *   - no a6xx_rpmh_start/warm boot: a6xx_gmu_rpmh_init() (RSCC + PDC) is
+ *     ported and runs once before the first GMU start, but the RPMh "start"
+ *     handshake and the GMU's own runtime votes are not;
+ *   - no GBIF halt, icache/dcache GMU buffers, HWCG tables, CP_PROTECT,
+ *     preemption or power-collapse counters beyond the few mainline writes
+ *     reproduced below;
+ *   - no per-process GPU VMs: SMMU CB0 keeps the identity map for PA 2-8 GB
+ *     (GPU/firmware/ring/scratch), CB1 gives the GMU (stream 5) its own
+ *     4 KB-granule stage-1 map for the debug/log/HFI buffers at IOVA
+ *     0x60000000 up, like mainline a6xx_gmu_memory_alloc(); an 8-16 GB window
+ *     covers client buffers, like the A530 driver.
+ */
